    "design": "vox-emphasis",
    "x_note": "Seventh film, seventh mock: Vox Emphasis Animator (Elements Annotator v0.4). The brief was the element use case itself — text with annotation — and the three marks it names: circle emphasis, the double-line rule, the highlighter. The double rule is new: `dbl-underline` was added to the shape vocabulary for this film, two draw-on strokes in a fixed-height strip under the words. Light mode, Inter (the mock's own face), zinc paper, one rose accent, and the mock's pen colours as the only other ink. Every product fact comes from reference/v0.4-perfect-.html — see NOTES.md."
  },
  "design": {
    "style": "vox emphasis",
    "x_note": "Zinc paper (the mock's own light canvas) with one rose accent for UI voice — the mock's export button is rose, and rose-600 rather than rose-500 so overlines clear AA as bold text. Every other saturated colour is a PEN: the circle colours, the rule amber and the highlighter tints are the mock's element-library hexes, used nowhere else. Like the sixth film, mark inks are tokens but not theme roles — a pen that re-themes mid-film is a different pen.",
    "tokens": {
      "bg": "#f4f4f5",
      "surface": "#ffffff",
      "surface-hi": "#e9e9ec",
      "on-surface": "#18181b",
      "on-variant": "#52525b",
